      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name} The issue is the new avatar details UI (introduced around the same time period as the Avatar Marketplace in May 2025) doesn't display content warnings. I always have to revert to clicking an user's pill in a world, then go to the old avatar details menu (the one without photo gallery and without custom tags) to see an avatar's content warnings. Worse, if that avatar is performance blocked, I have to temporarily show that other user's avatar first to navigate to the old avatar menu, else the option to access that old avatar details menu will be disabled (or replaced with \"fallback details\" if it's a fallback avatar).\n\nThis is not related to the open beta, by the way. This affects all avatars with content warnings. If an avatar doesn't have content warnings, then both of those avatar details UIs are indifferent as expected.",
